v 3
d mergemap: map the merges, appends and joins across your do-files
d
d mergemap reads a sequence of do-files and reports every merge, append,
d joinby, cross, frlink and frget in them, together with the reshaping and
d filtering steps around them.  By default it executes nothing: it reads the
d code the way you would read it and prints a numbered receipt of what it
d found.  Run mode executes the do-files with instrumentation and adds what
d actually happened -- observed cardinality, duplicate keys, the _merge
d breakdown, coverage on each side, and the most common unmatched keys.
d
d It answers one question: how did this dataset get built?  Useful when you
d inherit a project, when a merge has gone wrong and you need to find where,
d and when you need a record of a data pipeline for an appendix.
d
d This version draws: mergemap draw renders the map in the Results
d window, as self-contained HTML, as PNG/SVG through Stata graphs, or
d as mermaid/DOT text; mergemap sql teaches each join form as a row
d pairing.
d
d Start with: mergemap demo
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Eric Booth
d Support: email eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260821
